WEBVTT

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:14.110
Well, this is unusual.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:18.120
How long has it been since you've
shown yourself at POG Japan?

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.080
Come to turn in an overdue
letter of apology?

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:23.040
Me?

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.130
I've just delivered a humiliating report.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:29.130
Up till now, I had just
been warming up, but...

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:32.090
The most sacred of men are those who
create puzzles:

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:34.020
the POG's Givers.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:37.050
As one of them, and as Chief
of Far East Headquarters,

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.850
I have no business losing to a Solver.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.100
Yes?

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.890
Still, my next puzzle
will no doubt provide

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:47.380
Kaito Daimon with beautiful fear and death.

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:49.190
I'm sure of it.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:52.780
Here's the thing:

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:56.700
I've decided to lay the
next puzzle at Root Gakuen.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.250
It will be perfectly
suited for his demise.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.620
You will of course not refuse, yes?

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:04.750
Though your section may
have special privileges,

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.750
I am higher in rank than you.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:09.170
We understand each other, don't we?

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:11.670
Baron Kaidou?

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:19.180
Oh, well, I suppose it can't be helped.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.680
So, you allowed it?

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:27.730
There was no reason to object.

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:30.310
It looks like somebody troublesome
has taken an interest in him.

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:33.730
Is this another "trial"?

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:37.740
It's because they need
them to become stronger,

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.210
those who will challenge
the Puzzle of God,

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:42.240
the Phi-Brain children.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.660
We must make them grow.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:48.710
That is the purpose of this
POG special training institute,

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:51.410
the directive of Section Phi.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.870
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:15.600
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.450
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:20.190
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:24.700
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:29.410
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:31.630
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:34.280
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:36.290
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:38.590
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:40.530
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:43.350
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:47.850
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:50.150
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:54.840
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.060
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.400
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.030
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:07.920
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:13.600
Brain diver

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:18.400
Brain diver

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:26.970
The Fallen Apple & the
Path's Continuation

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:31.290
Root Gakuen
School Festival

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.060
Ta-daa!

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:35.650
Gah! Nonoha sweets!

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:38.570
Madeleine cakes?

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:41.990
They're the featured item at the
"Sub-Zero Coffee Shop" my class is doing.

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:43.610
They look delicious.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:44.840
Have some, have some!

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:46.080
No thanks, no thanks.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.660
What are you all doing
for the school festival?

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.700
I, Ana, will do an exhi...

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:54.500
I'm presenting my invention, Okabe No. 3.

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:57.630
Geniuses sure put on a production, huh?

00:03:58.160 --> 00:03:59.540
What about you, Gammon?

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:02.680
...se.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:03.720
Huh?

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:05.350
Hrnd hse.

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:06.720
Huh? What?

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.720
A haunted house!

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:13.690
Why do people gotta be scared
at a school festival?

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:15.540
It's in bad taste.

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:19.690
That's it, Nonoha.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:21.890
I'll help your class!

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:23.610
That'd be great!

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:26.880
I have to go help a lot of other clubs.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.580
There's the Ballet Club's
curry house at 10:30, right?

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:32.410
And at 10:35, the Swimming
Club's stew restaurant.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:35.920
At 10:40, I play a prince
for the Drama Club, right?

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:39.670
At 10:50, I cook roasted
eel for the Kabaddi Club.

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:43.420
At 10:55, there's the tournament with the
Girls' Pro Wrestling Club, right?

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:46.510
At 11:00, there's the
Soccer Club's ramen house.

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:46.520
As always, a needlessly good memory.

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:49.300
At 11:05, I model for
the Photography Club.

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:49.300
Well, just so long as you ain't around.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:52.430
At 11:10, I make dumplings
for the Lacrosse Club.

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:52.020
If you had to spend time
with this lugnut...

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:54.020
Oh, Kaito won't be around either.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.110
He has an important event.

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:59.030
'Cuz you friggin entered me into it.

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:01.190
What is this "Root Boy" thing anyway?!

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:04.060
A Miss Transvestite
competition! For boys only!

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:07.570
Come on, I bet girls'
clothes would suit you.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:09.330
They'd suit Ana more, right?!

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:18.580
No, no, no, no, no!

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:19.800
No, Ana is a no!

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:21.590
Cute, but no!

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:24.590
If it stirred some strange feelings in Kaito,
that would be bad!

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:27.330
I wanna see Kaito in girls' clothes!

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:28.760
No way!

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:30.600
Fine! I'll do it too!

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:31.600
What the hell for?!

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:35.180
There's someone I want
to see me as a girl.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:38.320
That makes no sense!

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:38.320
Daimon...

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:40.440
To think that you will
be participating...

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:45.400
The school fair is the perfect chance to address
all of your indignities up till now.

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:47.700
You fools again?

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:50.660
As winner of the Effort Award in last year's
Miss Root Gakuen Contest,

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:52.790
I shall best you in women's clothing!

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:53.460
Furthermore!

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:55.660
Mr. Takeda's latest
work, a special sudoku

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:59.210
made just for the fair, will destroy you!

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:01.920
It will be a flawless victory
for the Puzzle Club!

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:04.960
You're happy to beat him
using women's clothing?

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:08.550
As usual, that's an ugly sudoku.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:10.220
I look forward to seeing you in drag.

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:11.720
What?!

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:14.700
Fine, shall I change things up?

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:15.520
The president!

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:17.270
Upperclassman Jikukawa!

00:06:23.010 --> 00:06:23.970
There.

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:28.490
<i>This is pretty.</i>

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:33.240
<i>Student Council President
Souji Jikukawa...</i>

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:35.490
<i>Student Council President
Souji Jikukawa...</i>

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:37.160
Oh, jeez.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:40.120
Please return to the Fair
Action Committee at once.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.330
Being president sure makes you busy.

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:42.040
He turned that ugly sudoku

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:44.090
into a pretty puzzle in just a second.

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:48.790
He was the one who gave me
this computer thing too.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:52.850
Just who is he?

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:01.440
Yes, that's delicious!

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:05.170
This year's school festival looks
like it will be another hit.

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:10.610
My third school festival...

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.620
It's been two years now, huh?

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:28.760
I..It can't be!

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:35.390
I'm not fit to be a Phi-Brain, huh?

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:40.260
That was a strange thing to remember.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:44.150
Must be because of the setting
sun, red like an apple.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:47.610
<i>Hurry up and get back to work!</i>

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:49.110
<i>Upperclassman Jikukawa!</i>

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:52.030
<i>Souji Jikukawa!</i>

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:56.930
Root Gakuen
School Festival

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:13.240
Edison's Presentation

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:19.950
...was damaged.
Okabe No. 3:
FAILURE

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:25.600
How's this? Please?

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:26.730
Please?

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:29.140
M..Monster!

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:34.530
Bam! Here goes!

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:36.070
Just you wait, Nonoha.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:39.200
I will win, for you!

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:47.580
More rice, more!

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:49.590
They're steamed up...

00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:53.720
Things are rather busy, yes?

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:58.680
As a result, I can transport
this in with no one noticing.

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:03.480
Now, it shall begin,
Kaito Daimon's beautiful fear and death.

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:07.230
Kaito, your skin is so pretty!

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:09.610
Why did this happen to me?

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:11.810
Kaito, do your best!

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:13.560
I'll come by later to cheer you on.

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:14.550
Stay away!

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:16.020
That's no good.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:17.200
Stay still, please.

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:21.130
Next up, the Drama Club!

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:24.670
Ow...

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:26.250
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:31.840
Upperclassman, you're so pretty!

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:34.170
I look like a damn fool, don't I?

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:46.060
Successfully hacked.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:48.770
Using Nonoha, the chief of

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:52.070
the Far East Headquarters
sure is reckless.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:54.990
Is this another "trial"?

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:05.500
Miss Root Boy Contest

00:10:02.750 --> 00:10:05.930
Entry No. 3, Miss Takeda!

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:09.550
I'm back! I'm back! I'm back!

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:13.170
Miss Takeda, wo ai ni!

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:15.130
I wonder where he went?

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:17.090
Kaito...

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:26.350
This kind of thing, here at the Gakuen?

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:52.440
Nonoha!

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:56.050
<i>Welcome to this Philosopher's
Puzzle, princess.</i>

00:10:56.550 --> 00:11:01.550
<i>As you can see, the prince is asleep,
a spell having been cast on him.</i>

00:11:02.420 --> 00:11:04.560
<i>In order to save him,</i>

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:08.640
<i>you must feed him the Delicious Apples
that these dwarves hold.</i>

00:11:09.450 --> 00:11:11.480
<i>But be careful:</i>

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:15.150
<i>Only dwarves from the
honest group that always</i>

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:18.340
<i>
tell the truth hold Delicious Apples.</i>

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:21.240
<i>The dwarves from the lying group that</i>

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:23.320
<i>
only tell lies hold poison apples.</i>

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:25.940
Honesty and lies...

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:27.830
This is a logic puzzle, huh?

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:31.240
<i>Exactly, a puzzle without
form, where answers</i>

00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:33.480
<i>
are discerned through conversation.</i>

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:35.340
<i>Such is this logic puzzle.</i>

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:39.210
<i>If you can find all the Delicious Apples,</i>

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:41.340
<i>
the prince will be released.</i>

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:48.590
<i>That is, if you can find them
before you burn to a crisp.</i>

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:51.020
You son of a bitch!

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:52.770
Now then, let's begin.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:55.650
The riddles will only be spoken once.

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:57.020
Listen closely.

00:11:57.020 --> 00:12:00.530
<i>The Black Dwarf has a Delicious Apple.</i>

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:03.530
<i>I dug up gold nuggets!</i>

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:06.030
<i>I'm in the same group
as the Orange Dwarf.</i>

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:08.600
<i>The weather in the
mountains changes often.</i>

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:10.040
<i>It rained heavily yesterday.</i>

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:12.790
<i>I'm not in the same group
as the White Dwarf.</i>

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:15.540
<i>I ain't in the same group
as that Green Dwarf.</i>

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:19.130
<i>The Red Dwarf holds a Delicious Apple.</i>

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:22.880
<i>Well, which are the Delicious Apples?!</i>

00:12:23.240 --> 00:12:25.140
Wait, Nonoha!

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:27.010
I'm on my way!

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:30.270
Puzzle time, let's begin!

00:12:31.070 --> 00:12:33.950
A logic puzzle using apples, huh?

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:38.270
This is...

00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:46.840
What the hell?

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:49.150
No matter how much I try,
I can't see the answer!

00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:52.410
I gotta think again,
from the beginning...

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:55.620
<i>I'm in the same group
as the Orange Dwarf.</i>

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:58.550
If I assume the Yellow Dwarf
is in the lying group,

00:12:58.550 --> 00:13:00.460
then him being in the
same group is a lie.

00:13:00.940 --> 00:13:04.680
That means that Orange, unlike Yellow,
is in the truthful group.

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:08.400
But if I assume Yellow is
in the truthful group...

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:11.780
In that case, he really
is in the same group,

00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:15.390
and Orange and Yellow are
both in the truthful group.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:19.190
In either case, Orange
is in the truthful group,

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:22.940
so Orange is holding a Delicious Apple!

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:28.200
<i>The White Dwarf isn't in the same group.</i>

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:30.200
If I go with this line of thinking,

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:33.860
and Blue is in the lying
group, then White is a liar.

00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:37.210
And if he is truthful,
White is still a liar.

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:40.090
In either case, White is a liar.

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:41.840
He's holding a poison apple.

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:44.720
<i>I ain't in the same group
as that Green Dwarf.</i>

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:46.720
By the same logic...

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:48.970
Green is in the lying group too.

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:52.470
<i>The Red Dwarf holds a Delicious Apple.</i>

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:56.060
I've just learned that White
is in the lying group,

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:58.060
so this is a lie!

00:13:58.060 --> 00:13:59.980
Red is holding a poison apple!

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:03.230
<i>The Black Dwarf has a Delicious Apple.</i>

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:05.600
Red's in the lying group too,

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:08.240
so Black has a poison apple too!

00:14:08.630 --> 00:14:11.200
In other words, the lying group is...

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:14.500
Red, Green, Black and White!

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:16.750
They're holding poison apples.

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:21.040
And the Delicious Apples are held
by the truthful dwarves,

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:22.040
Orange and...

00:14:23.390 --> 00:14:25.050
No, I don't get it.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:27.130
If there's one Delicious Apple,

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:29.180
then the answer is, the
apple that Orange holds.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:30.480
If there are three,

00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:33.580
then they're the ones that Orange,
Yellow and Blue hold.

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:35.020
But if there are two...

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:38.630
How many Delicious Apples are there?

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:42.060
Unless I know that, I
can't get just one answer!

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:47.680
There's no more time!

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:50.200
Something...

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:53.330
Is there something
important I'm not seeing?

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:57.280
Such beautiful flames...

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:02.040
Tremble, fear and then die,

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:04.040
Kaito Daimon.

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:12.180
Nonoha!

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:13.550
Dammit!

00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:18.060
Why? Why can't I see the answer?!

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:20.270
Don't tell me this puzzle...

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:24.630
It doesn't give you all the information!

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:32.140
THAT IS CORRECT

00:15:34.070 --> 00:15:36.160
This is from Minotaur!

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:39.620
"This puzzle intentionally
withholds information

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:41.670
that by rights should be provided."

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:44.000
"Thus, I shall intervene in this puzzle

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:45.320
and put things as they were."

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:46.920
What the heck?

00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:51.670
You're a POG Giver!

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:53.930
Why would you do something like that?!

00:15:53.950 --> 00:16:00.910
A PUZZLE MADE ONLY TO KILL SOMEONE
IS NOT BEAUTIFUL...
CORRECT?

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:06.110
"Not being able to see the puzzle's
flaw was the Solver's mistake."

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:09.580
The chief probably intended
to use that as an excuse.

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:11.810
Something like that...

00:16:11.810 --> 00:16:15.760
If it's not even a trial, it
is not a Philosopher's Puzzle.

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:20.080
<i>Will you not accept?</i>

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:22.330
<i>True, as a Solver, you did not possess</i>

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:24.910
<i>the qualities of a Phi-Brain.</i>

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:27.000
<i>But in becoming a Giver,</i>

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:29.720
<i>you have been given great possibilities.</i>

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:32.170
<i>That is what I think.</i>

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:35.720
<i>The fundamental wish of
the Philosopher's Puzzles</i>

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:38.210
<i>was to keep a prize sealed,</i>

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:42.060
<i>but also to reward those
who possessed skill.</i>

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:45.500
<i>They were imbued with the
conflicting will of their client.</i>

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:49.070
<i>But the puzzles the POG make now</i>

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:52.320
<i>can hardly be called puzzles,
they're little more than deathtraps.</i>

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:54.560
<i>Light and darkness.</i>

00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:56.710
<i>Hope and despair.</i>

00:16:56.710 --> 00:16:59.900
<i>Giver and Solver, knowing both,</i>

00:16:59.900 --> 00:17:02.080
<i>you can make true Philosophers' Puzzles.</i>

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:04.670
<i>And eventually, you can
guide the Phi-Brain children</i>

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:08.630
<i>to properly solve the Puzzle of God.</i>

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:11.170
<i>Such is my thinking.</i>

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:28.060
I can't just let them be killed by
some incomplete puzzle!

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:29.110
My desires...

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:30.110
My dreams!

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:33.650
And my dear underclassman!

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:38.590
Delicious Apples...

00:17:38.590 --> 00:17:39.870
Delicious Apples!

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:41.620
There are three of them!

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:43.750
That's the information I needed, huh?!

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:47.000
In that case, I see the answer!

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:52.630
The truthful dwarves are
Orange, Yellow and Blue!

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:56.630
The three apples they hold
are Delicious Apples!

00:17:56.630 --> 00:17:58.890
<i>Correct!</i>

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:01.760
Nonoha!

00:18:01.880 --> 00:18:03.190
Im..Impossible!

00:18:03.190 --> 00:18:06.400
Someone intervened in my puzzle? Who?!

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:11.020
No matter.

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:13.150
You're already too late.

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:19.740
I took too much time?!

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:34.300
I'm glad we made it in time.

00:18:37.370 --> 00:18:40.760
I couldn't let something happen to
my precious underclassman.

00:18:44.670 --> 00:18:48.100
Why?! Why didn't he die?

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:50.810
It was the perfect strategy!

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:53.060
Getting in the way of my plan...

00:18:53.060 --> 00:18:55.160
Who are these fools?!

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:57.690
The Phi-Brain children.

00:18:58.440 --> 00:19:01.570
Now then, it is almost the
school festival's finale.

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:04.200
This time is for the students only.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:07.960
Be careful on your way back, Mr. Chief.

00:19:18.910 --> 00:19:21.760
That's my Okabe No. 3 all right!

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:23.760
It was a great success!

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:23.740
Failure
Great Success

00:19:24.380 --> 00:19:27.690
How did something like this
suddenly get built here?

00:19:27.690 --> 00:19:29.420
That's the POG for you.

00:19:29.420 --> 00:19:31.270
Oh my, that's bad.

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:34.770
But you solved it,
didn't you? The puzzle?

00:19:35.300 --> 00:19:36.530
I guess...

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:42.390
Nonoha!

00:19:42.390 --> 00:19:44.720
What about the Miss Root Boy Contest?

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:46.870
That's what's more important?

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:51.180
<i>And now, the voting results!</i>

00:19:51.180 --> 00:19:54.720
<i>The winner of this year's
Miss Root Boy Contest is...</i>

00:19:58.940 --> 00:20:01.540
<i>None other than Ana Gram!</i>

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:05.920
He ain't even a participant!

00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:07.390
Gammon!

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:15.370
<i>A puzzle made only to kill someone...</i>

00:20:15.370 --> 00:20:19.310
<i>Minotaur made it into a
proper, pretty puzzle.</i>

00:20:20.590 --> 00:20:21.920
<i>I don't get it.</i>

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:23.320
<i>Why did he...</i>

00:20:24.470 --> 00:20:27.330
Ah, Nonoha, so this is where you are!

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:29.610
Oh, that's right.

00:20:29.610 --> 00:20:32.480
Everyone, I'm sorry I couldn't go!

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:34.080
It's fine, really, fine.

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:36.350
The student council president helped us.

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:38.590
Huh? Upperclassman Jikukawa did?

00:20:38.590 --> 00:20:41.150
With playing the prince too.

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:43.610
And with the girls' pro wrestling match.

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:45.720
And with Sub-Zero Café's
Madeleine cakes.

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:48.390
He helped us with all of them.

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:50.720
Upperclassman Jikukawa is great!

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:54.230
<i>I don't really get him either.</i>

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:57.730
You acted quite recklessly.

00:20:57.730 --> 00:21:00.790
Hacking into the chief's computer.

00:21:00.790 --> 00:21:02.970
Intervening in a puzzle.

00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:07.200
These are all counter
to the POG's charters.

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:11.500
The puzzle the chief made was itself
counter to the POG's charters.

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:15.530
There was no sealed prize,
nor any regard for the person trapped within it.

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:18.460
A puzzle that serves only to kill someone

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:21.000
can't be called a Philosopher's Puzzle.

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:26.470
It would cause quite the
uproar it were learned

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:28.580
you are a member of our section.

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:33.470
But no matter, let us
overlook it this time.

00:21:33.470 --> 00:21:35.740
I shall clean things up on my end.

00:21:36.240 --> 00:21:37.730
Thank you very much.

00:21:38.180 --> 00:21:40.790
However, your performance was exemplary.

00:21:40.790 --> 00:21:43.990
Worthy of one holding the
title of "Newton," indeed.

00:21:44.330 --> 00:21:47.130
Having taken that title,

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:50.990
I couldn't let slide a puzzle
that misused apples, could I?

00:21:51.290 --> 00:21:53.660
It is a boon, having a straightforward,

00:21:53.660 --> 00:21:56.750
gifted student council president like you.

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:58.760
It's my way of giving thanks.

00:21:58.760 --> 00:22:03.090
To you, Mr. Principal, for
giving me new life as a Giver.

00:22:03.090 --> 00:22:04.510
Also...

00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:08.610
I don't hate my current position.

00:22:09.460 --> 00:22:13.620
The Solvers I've reared will
solve the Puzzle of God.

00:22:13.620 --> 00:22:16.520
I may be able to stand
present at that moment.

00:22:18.010 --> 00:22:20.730
Guiding them toward being Phi-Brains...

00:22:21.210 --> 00:22:24.490
That is the directive of us
in Section Phi, isn't it?

00:22:26.670 --> 00:22:28.110
Yes, it is.

00:22:37.270 --> 00:22:41.490
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.490 --> 00:22:47.410
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.410 --> 00:22:52.040
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.040 --> 00:22:57.090
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:02.570
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.570 --> 00:23:07.930
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:13.110
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.110 --> 00:23:18.360
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.360 --> 00:23:23.700
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:23.700 --> 00:23:26.380
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:29.290
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.290 --> 00:23:33.860
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.860 --> 00:23:39.160
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.160 --> 00:23:44.440
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.440 --> 00:23:49.980
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:49.980 --> 00:23:58.920
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:03.170 --> 00:24:05.250
Erena Himekawa sure is cute, huh?

00:24:05.250 --> 00:24:07.570
Couldn't tell ya! Who's that?!

00:24:07.570 --> 00:24:10.260
She's a 14-year-old intellectual starlet.

00:24:10.260 --> 00:24:12.680
She's cute, and she can solve puzzles.

00:24:12.680 --> 00:24:14.500
She really is perfect!

00:24:14.500 --> 00:24:17.720
But ain't bein' pegged
"intellectual" kinda dumb?

00:24:17.720 --> 00:24:20.180
Like, don't ya think she's really dumb?!

00:24:20.180 --> 00:24:22.740
Next time: "Welcome to
the Queen's Country"

00:24:21.410 --> 00:24:27.210
Welcome to the Queen's Country

00:24:22.740 --> 00:24:24.290
You truly are rude!

00:24:24.290 --> 00:24:27.360
Through my puzzles, you
shall know your place!
